          <notesStmt>
            <note>The advertisement names the instrument only as “Mignon“; the name
              Welte is not printed. It is identified as the Welte-Mignon by the
              picture of the cabinet player (the same block as in Grøndahl's
              "Welte-Mignon Reproduktionsklaver" advertisement in Aftenposten,
              January 10, 1908) and by the electric drive. A differently worded
              setting appeared in Morgenbladet on the same day.</note>
